    "state": "Madhya Pradesh",
    "description": "The Jai Vilas Palace is a nineteenth-century palace in Gwalior, India. It was built in 1874 by Jayajirao Scindia, the Maharaja of Gwalior in the British Raj. While the major part of the palace is now the \"Jiwajirao Scindia Museum\" which opened to the public in 1964, a part of it is still the residence of some of his descendants.",
